      "content": "**RootRef › Remove component**\n\nThis component has been removed.\n\nYou can get a reference to the underlying DOM node of our components via `ref` prop.\n\nThe component relied on [`ReactDOM.findDOMNode`](https://react.dev/reference/react-dom/findDOMNode) which is [deprecated in `React.StrictMode`](https://react.dev/reference/react/StrictMode#warning-about-deprecated-finddomnode-usage).\n\n:::success\nThis is handled in the [preset-safe codemod](#preset-safe) by applying fake `RootRef` component to prevent application crash, but further fixes are required.\n:::\n\n```diff\n-<RootRef rootRef={ref}>\n-  <Button />\n-</RootRef>\n+<Button ref={ref} />\n```\n\n---\n\n**ref › Refactor non-ref-forwarding class components**\n\nSupport for non-ref-forwarding class components in the `component` prop or as immediate `children` has been dropped.\n\nIf you were using `unstable_createStrictModeTheme` or didn't see any warnings related to `findDOMNode` in `React.StrictMode` then you don't need to take any further action.\n\nOtherwise check out the [Caveat with refs](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/guides/composition/#caveat-with-refs) section in the Composition guide to find out how to migrate.\nThis change affects almost all components where you're using the `component` prop or passing `children` to components that require `children` to be elements (for example `<MenuList><CustomMenuItem /></MenuList>`).\n\n---\n\n**ref › Fix ref type specificity**\n\nFor some components, you may get a type error when passing `ref`.\nTo avoid the error, you should use a specific element type.\nFor example, `Card` expects the type of `ref` to be `HTMLDivElement`, and `ListItem` expects its `ref` type to be `HTMLLIElement`.\n\nHere is an example:\n\n```diff\n import * as React from 'react';\n import Card from '@mui/material/Card';\n import ListItem from '@mui/material/ListItem';\n\n export default function SpecificRefType() {\n-  const cardRef = React.useRef<HTMLElement>(null);\n+  const cardRef = React.useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n\n-  const listItemRef = React.useRef<HTMLElement>(null);\n+  const listItemRef = React.useRef<HTMLLIElement>(null);\n   return (\n     <div>\n       <Card ref={cardRef}></Card>\n       <ListItem ref={listItemRef}></ListItem>\n     </div>\n   );\n }\n```\n\nHere are the specific element types that each component expects:\n\n#### @mui/material\n\n- [Accordion](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/accordion/) - `HTMLDivElement`\n- [Alert](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/alert/) - `HTMLDivElement`\n- [Avatar](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/avatar/) - `HTMLDivElement`\n- [ButtonGroup](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/button-group/) - `HTMLDivElement`\n- [Card](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/card/) - `HTMLDivElement`\n- [Dialog](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/dialog/) - `HTMLDivElement`\n- [ImageList](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/image-list/) - `HTMLUListElement`\n- [List](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/list/) - `HTMLUListElement`\n- [Tab](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/tab/) - `HTMLDivElement`\n- [Tabs](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/tabs/) - `HTMLDivElement`\n- [ToggleButton](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/toggle-button/) - `HTMLButtonElement`\n\n#### @mui/lab\n\n- [Timeline](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/timeline/) - `HTMLUListElement`",
